action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P80 on Windows: the `hover` verb, which reads back the cursor the platform draws
# at a point -- the only externally observable thing BackendFeatures.Cursors
# produces. Written 2026-10-07 with the Win32 implementation of the verb.
# Positions are the six labels' centres in a window capture of P80 (WinUI). The
# last row is the control: a plain label OUTSIDE every cursor target must read
# arrow, which is what shows each shape belongs to its view, not the window.
# P80(Windows):`hover` 讀回平台在某一點畫的游標。最後一列是對照：任何游標 target 之外的普通標籤必須讀到
# arrow,證明每個形狀屬於它的 view,而不是整個視窗。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let P80 lay out,windows
hover,174,228,frame,,,,hand label -- must report pointingHand,windows
hover,214,228,frame,,,,cross label -- must report crosshair,windows
hover,249,228,frame,,,,text label -- must report text,windows
hover,276,228,frame,,,,left-right label -- must report resizeHorizontal,windows
hover,296,228,frame,,,,up-down label -- must report resizeVertical,windows
hover,320,228,frame,,,,no label -- must report notAllowed,windows
hover,220,202,frame,,,,"the 'cursors -- hover each:' label, outside every target -- must report arrow",windows
